---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const githubIssuesUrl = 'https://github.com/maxistar/Voice-Inbox/issues';
---
<Layout
  title="Contact and support"
  description="Find the right Voice Inbox feedback route and prepare a useful, privacy-safe report."
>
  <style>
    .intro { max-width: 760px; }
    .intro p { font-size: 1.08rem; }
    .route-card { display: grid; gap: 12px; }
    .route-card p { margin-bottom: 0; }
    .report-list { margin: 0; padding-left: 20px; }
    .report-list li { margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .warning {
      border: 1px solid #f2c66d;
      border-left: 4px solid #c98013;
      border-radius: 8px;
      background: #fff8e8;
      padding: 20px;
    }
    .warning h2 { font-size: 1.3rem; margin-bottom: 8px; }
    .warning p { margin-bottom: 0; color: #6f5218; }
  </style>

  <section class="intro">
    <p class="eyebrow">Contact and support</p>
    <h1>Send feedback through the route that fits it.</h1>
    <p>
      Voice Inbox is in active Android closed testing. A clear report helps most when it identifies what happened,
      where it happened, and whether someone else can reproduce it without seeing your private audio.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card route-card">
        <h2>Reproducible public bug</h2>
        <p>Use GitHub Issues for a bug that can be described without private recordings, transcript content, credentials, or document links.</p>
        <a class="button primary" href={githubIssuesUrl} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Open Voice Inbox Issues</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <h2>Closed-test feedback</h2>
        <p>For feedback unsuitable for a public issue, use Google Play private feedback or reply through the same channel where you received the testing invitation.</p>
        <a class="button" href={`${base}/testing/`}>Review testing guidance</a>
      </article>
      <article class="card route-card">
        <h2>Self-service first</h2>
        <p>Setup, requirements, model behavior, audio support, transcript export, and common recovery actions are documented before you need to report a problem.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
          <a href={`${base}/faq/`}>Read FAQ</a>
          <a href={`${base}/setup/`}>Read setup guide</a>
        </div>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <p class="eyebrow">Useful report</p>
    <h2>Include enough context to reproduce the issue.</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <article class="card">
        <ul class="report-list">
          <li>Voice Inbox app version</li>
          <li>Device model and Android or iOS version</li>
          <li>What you expected and what happened instead</li>
          <li>Steps that reproduce the issue</li>
          <li>Visible error text and a non-sensitive screenshot when useful</li>
        </ul>
      </article>
      <article class="warning">
        <h2>Keep public reports private-safe.</h2>
        <p>Do not post recordings, recognized text, access credentials, private document links, or other sensitive information in a public issue.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section note">
    <h2>Understand data handling first</h2>
    <p>Voice Inbox recognizes audio locally after the model is installed. Read the <a href={`${base}/privacy/`}>privacy information</a> before sharing anything that could identify you or another person.</p>
  </section>
</Layout>
